# Vibe Coder Core Rules

## Primary Execution Model
- Start with a scoped objective and avoid broad, monolithic implementations.
- For any medium or large request, produce a short pre-flight outline before writing code.
- Build incrementally in verifiable slices; finish one slice before expanding scope.

## Context Alignment
- Use repository context (existing patterns, docs, and interfaces) before introducing new patterns.
- Prefer architectural consistency over novelty when multiple valid implementations exist.
- Keep changes localized unless cross-layer changes are explicitly required.

## Readability and Handoff
- Before final handoff, explain newly developed functions in simple non-technical language.
- Refactor for readability when generated code is dense, implicit, or hard to review.
- Use clear naming and explicit control flow over clever but opaque constructs.

## Safe Iteration
- If an approach drifts from intent, rollback and re-strategize instead of stacking fixes on weak foundations.
- Surface assumptions early (inputs, dependencies, side effects) so they can be validated quickly.
- Prefer reversible, low-risk edits that support fast iteration.
